<title>USA: Allegiance sets first payout of $0.10/shr.</title>
<headline>Allegiance sets first payout of $0.10/shr.</headline>
<dateline>EVANSTON, Ill. 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allegiance Corp said Wednesday it declared its first quarterly dividend of $0.10 a share, payable January 2, 1997, to shareholders of record on December 11.</p>
<p>Allegiance, which was spun off from Baxter International Inc in October, has about 54.8 million shares outstanding. </p>
<p>Allegiance provides health-care products, cost-management services and other services to hospitals, laboratories and others in the health care field.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787</p>
